{"The device limit check has a Time-Of-Check to Time-Of-Use (TOCTOU) race condition where multiple concurrent requests can evaluate the device count before any new devices are inserted, all finding the count below the limit and proceeding to insert, effectively bypassing the anonymous device limit": 0.880247950553894, "When the device limit is reached, Anonymous.Authenticate returns a plain error that becomes an authentication failure, but there is no dedicated HTTP/status mapping for this condition, so clients will experience generic unauthenticated behavior rather than a clear 'device limit reached' response": 0.660677969455719, "ProvideAnonDBStore is still registered in wire.go but its signature now requires an int64 parameter that wire cannot inject, and since ProvideAnonymousDeviceService now takes db.DB instead of anonstore.AnonStore and creates the store internally, the wire provider and its interface binding are orphaned, causing wire code generation to fail": 0.7386434674263, "TagDevice was previously called in a fire-and-forget goroutine with a dedicated 2-minute timeout and panic recovery, but is now called synchronously on the request context, adding 1-2 database round-trips to every anonymous authentication response and removing the panic safety net that previously protected the auth path": 0.9473900198936462}